  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecumenical Peace Observation Initiative in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Throughout Zimbabwe&#x2019;s turbulent history, the Church has played key roles in mediation, peace building and conflict resolution.  It has also exercised its prophetic voice to expose human rights abuses and point out the excesses of the state. Under the auspices of the Heads of Christian Denominations (HOCD) the Church has since 2003 been working in a more coordinated way to help resolve the political, social and economic crisis in Zimbabwe. The Church has also played a key role in the setting up of other specialized agencies that operate at different levels. These include the Zimbabwe Election Support Network (ZESN) and the Zimbabwe Peace Project (ZPP).</narrative>
  </description>
